# LinkedIn posts — no duplicates

Before drafting any LinkedIn post (including dry runs), search existing `runs/**/post*.md`.

## Block if any prior post already has

- The same core claim or takeaway (reworded counts)
- The same hook idea (e.g. “AI did not start with ChatGPT”)
- The same topic + angle (e.g. another History-of-AI timeline recap)
- A compressed remake of an existing series episode

Exact wording match is not required. Theme overlap is enough to reject.

## Required workflow

1. Grep/search `runs/` for the intended hook, claim, and key terms.
2. Skim recent and series posts if the topic is History of AI, full-stack, or a recurring theme.
3. Only then draft a **new** angle.
4. If the idea is already covered, pick a different topic — do not rewrite the same post.

## Examples

- Bad: New post “ChatGPT is not year zero of AI” when `runs/2026-08-28/post.md` already says AI did not start with ChatGPT.
- Good: Same sheet source, but a unused angle (e.g. MYCIN demo≠production, Chinchilla, ELIZA Effect) that no prior `post*.md` covers.

Never ask the user to remind you; always check `runs/` first.
